Aurora on the browser's WebGPU (emdawnwebgpu) and SDL3 (Emscripten port)

BlueWake web port (web/), applied by web/build.sh to a worktree of the pinned
RecompCore in build/web/recompcore; every change is limited to __EMSCRIPTEN__
or EMSCRIPTEN, so other builds compile as before.

- aurora_core/aurora_gx: no WEBGPU_DAWN and no Dawn window binding or Tracy
  platform: webgpu.h is emdawnwebgpu over the page's WebGPU.
- extern: ImGui 1.91's Dawn code path fits emdawnwebgpu, which is Dawn's own
  webgpu.h, but under __EMSCRIPTEN__ its backend expects Emscripten's older
  bindings: imgui_impl_wgpu.cpp is compiled without __EMSCRIPTEN__.
- gpu.cpp: the surface is the page's canvas (#canvas, transferred to the
  worker); a Core adapter (a browser may hand out a reduced compatibility-mode
  adapter when asked for Compatibility); Dawn's logging callbacks only with
  Dawn.
- render_worker: not started in a browser, where a WebGPU device and its
  objects belong to the thread that made them; items run where queued (the
  existing path before initialize()), with the thread counted as the render
  worker while it runs one, as the checks in the work expect.
- common.cpp, texture.cpp: waits for a buffer map suspend to the event loop
  (emscripten_sleep), the only place a browser completes one; sleeping in
  place waited forever.
- aurora.cpp: present is a JSPI suspension (emscripten_sleep(0)): the browser
  shows the canvas's frame when its thread returns to the event loop, and
  emdawnwebgpu has no wgpuSurfacePresent.
- rmlui.hpp: <webgpu/webgpu_cpp.h>, as the rest of Aurora includes it.
- dds_io.cpp, texture_replacement.cpp: texture sizes cast to size_t (32-bit).
- aurora_graphics.cpp: no backtrace()/thread-signal stall stacks (as on
  Windows; DOL_GX_STALL_STACKS is a Mac and Linux diagnostic).

